<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong class=3D"example">Example 1:</strong></p>

<pre><strong>Input:</strong> nums =3D [-2,1,-3,4,-1,2,1,-5,4]
<strong>Output:</strong> 6
<strong>Explanation:</strong> The subarray [4,-1,2,1] has the largest sum 6=
.
</pre>

<p><strong class=3D"example">Example 2:</strong></p>

<pre><strong>Input:</strong> nums =3D [1]
<strong>Output:</strong> 1
<strong>Explanation:</strong> The subarray [1] has the largest sum 1.
</pre>

<p><strong class=3D"example">Example 3:</strong></p>

<pre><strong>Input:</strong> nums =3D [5,4,-1,7,8]
<strong>Output:</strong> 23
<strong>Explanation:</strong> The subarray [5,4,-1,7,8] has the largest sum=
 23.
</pre>

<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong>Constraints:</strong></p>

<ul>
	<li><code>1 &lt;=3D nums.length &lt;=3D 10<sup>5</sup></code></li>
	<li><code>-10<sup>4</sup> &lt;=3D nums[i] &lt;=3D 10<sup>4</sup></code></l=
i>
</ul>

